<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 19:54:33 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Only the beginning? German far-right's breakthrough shakes Europe to its core</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260907-only-the-beginning-german-far-right-s-breakthrough-shakes-europe-to-its-core</link><description>
Not enough to win outright but enough to shake Germany and Europe to their core: the far-right Alterniv für Deutschland trouncing the ruling conservatives in the impoverished former East German region of Saxony-Anhalt. We’ll ask about the consequences of voting for an anti-immigrant, pro-Russian party that wants schools to teach less about the ills of Hitler and more the glory of Bismarck.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/23ca6038-aae5-11f1-ba8f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-07T171919Z-1548302850-RC2HENA17DPG-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/23ca6038-aae5-11f1-ba8f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-07T171919Z-1548302850-RC2HENA17DPG-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2c88cdb8-aae5-11f1-b077-4fa18040d678</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 19:38:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'What we see right now is that Putin has zero interest in ending the war', Ukrainian MP Yasko says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says</link><description>
US envoy Steve Witkoff on Monday touted progress in weekend discussions with Ukraine and Russia, raising the prospect of reviving three-way peace talks to end Europe's deadliest conflict since World War II. Ukrainian MP Lisa Yasko says that "we don't trust these talks", describing the US envoys' flattery towards Russian President Vladimir Putin as "disgraceful".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2931813c-aaea-11f1-a276-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-200740-201844-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2931813c-aaea-11f1-a276-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-200740-201844-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e57ec64-aaea-11f1-bdbe-4fa18040d678</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:38:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Avalanche kills at least 11 climbers in southern Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia</link><description>
⁠At least ​11 people were killed and six ​others injured after an avalanche struck a group of climbers in Russia's ​southern Kabardino-Balkaria ‌Republic, local emergency services said. The ‌avalanche swept down Mount Mizhirgi, ⁠one of the highest peaks in Russia's North Caucasus.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37b2dd78-aacc-11f1-ac97-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/miniaalane.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37b2dd78-aacc-11f1-ac97-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/miniaalane.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e95feee-aacc-11f1-8328-2b49e65c2de6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 15:00:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1</link><description>
Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a1ef7e-aac2-11f1-ad2d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150057-150748-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a1ef7e-aac2-11f1-ad2d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150057-150748-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a99d2b1e-aac2-11f1-b13f-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:01:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd</link><description>
Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d78d6c00-aab8-11f1-8074-bb94302a716d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:45:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg">© Matthias Schrader, AP</source><dc:creator>Simon FEISTHAUER FOURNET</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d5e75d2-aab6-11f1-bc26-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-130059-131732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d5e75d2-aab6-11f1-bc26-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-130059-131732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b23d92-aab6-11f1-9063-ff9d54eec782</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:41:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'Jubilation and pain': German far right marches to victory in key state election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 7: The far right marches to victory in a German state election: what does this mean for the future of Germany and Europe at large? Also: the Daily Telegraph publishes an exclusive interview with the sons of former Pakistani PM Imran Khan about his imprisonment conditions in Pakistan. Plus the US Open descends into chaos after influencers, weed and disruptions stir controversy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66bad82a-aaa2-11f1-ae88-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3818120436a9e8a4e715ec8-42611865.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66bad82a-aaa2-11f1-ae88-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3818120436a9e8a4e715ec8-42611865.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78efaf8e-aa84-11f1-a013-23a43548d837</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 10:05:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany seeks to dismiss Nicaragua's Gaza genocide case at top UN court</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court</link><description>
Germany is set to ask the International Court of Justice on Monday to dismiss a case accusing Berlin of "facilitating genocide" in Gaza by supporting Israel after the deadly October 7, 2023 attacks by Hamas militants. The details of the case, filed by Nicaragua in 2024, have not yet been made public.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd88d198-aa98-11f1-bbc1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24121478760179.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd88d198-aa98-11f1-bbc1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24121478760179.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b4046a4-aa99-11f1-ad8f-9365a386766e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 09:14:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd88d198-aa98-11f1-bbc1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24121478760179.jpg">© Peter Dejong, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Thousands of mourners gather in Belgrade for war criminal Mladic's funeral</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-thousands-of-mourners-gather-in-belgrade-for-war-criminal-mladic-s-funeral</link><description>
Thousands of mourners on Monday gathered at a church in Belgrade for the funeral of Ratko Mladic, who died in The Hague, Netherlands, on August 27 while serving a life sentence for genocide, war crimes and crimes against humanity. The European Union heavily criticised the decision to hold a public funeral service with Marta Kos, the bloc's enlargement commissioner, having cancelled an upcoming visit to Serbia in protest. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2bbba572-aa90-11f1-a958-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250196078380.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2bbba572-aa90-11f1-a958-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250196078380.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf2ec650-aa8f-11f1-be3c-3799561a2960</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 08:08:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2bbba572-aa90-11f1-a958-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250196078380.jpg">© Marko Drobnjakovic, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Germany’s Merz 'deeply shocked' by far-right AfD's historic electoral victory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-live-europe-reacts-to-germany-far-right-afd-worrying-electoral-victory</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz told the press on Monday that he was "deeply shocked" by the far-right AfD's historic victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election a day earlier. The AfD is labelled a "right-wing extremist" group by Germany's domestic intelligence agency, and some of its staff are former members of a since-banned neo-Nazi organisation. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f697102-aab3-11f1-8fe2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-07T115411Z-2095087364-RC2BENATRNZW-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-CDU-REACTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f697102-aab3-11f1-8fe2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-07T115411Z-2095087364-RC2BENATRNZW-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-CDU-REACTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9a54242-aa84-11f1-af5d-23a43548d837</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 06:30:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f697102-aab3-11f1-8fe2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-07T115411Z-2095087364-RC2BENATRNZW-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-CDU-REACTION.jpg">© Axel Schmidt, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany's Merz vows to stick with reforms despite election drubbing by far right</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-s-merz-shocked-by-far-right-state-win-but-vows-to-stay-course</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Monday vowed to press ahead with his reform agenda despite a blistering election defeat for his centre-right CDU in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right AfD won almost 44 percent of the vote. Merz called the result his party’s worst defeat in decades.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fedf184-aabd-11f1-8f20-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/372fc877cdbd4f9c9c165df583c11cd09d9aa532.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fedf184-aabd-11f1-8f20-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/372fc877cdbd4f9c9c165df583c11cd09d9aa532.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cabd7538-aa7c-11f1-afc2-fd5898949920</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 05:27:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fedf184-aabd-11f1-8f20-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/372fc877cdbd4f9c9c165df583c11cd09d9aa532.jpg">© Ralf Hirschberger, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US envoys bring ‘more effective’ Ukraine peace proposals to Kyiv, official says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-us-envoys-more-effective-ukraine-peace-proposals-kyiv</link><description>
US envoys brought new, “more effective” proposals to Kyiv aimed at ending the war with Russia, a senior Ukrainian presidential official said on Sunday. President Volodymyr Zelensky and US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner described talks positively but announced no breakthrough, as Zelensky warned fighting could continue into winter.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b48393d2-aa46-11f1-93e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7H37XW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b48393d2-aa46-11f1-93e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7H37XW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a190da30-aa43-11f1-9734-cb49e6b6ff4e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:31:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b48393d2-aa46-11f1-93e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7H37XW.jpg">© Genya Savilov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU to boost Greenland investment amid Trump annexation claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-eu-greenland-investment-trump-annexation</link><description>
European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen is expected to announce increased EU investment in Greenland on Monday, including in critical minerals, satellite communications and renewable energy. Her two-day visit signals support for Greenland and Denmark amid US President Donald Trump’s push for American control of the Arctic territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86f4fb1a-aa35-11f1-b2ef-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9d61d00159832049328fe4c415db3ad2e341d18c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86f4fb1a-aa35-11f1-b2ef-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9d61d00159832049328fe4c415db3ad2e341d18c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f53410b0-aa4f-11f1-a23c-f1d561d257af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:27:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86f4fb1a-aa35-11f1-b2ef-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9d61d00159832049328fe4c415db3ad2e341d18c.jpg">© Mads Claus Rasmussen, Ritzau Scanpix, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Ready to talk': German far right celebrates victory in Saxony-Anhalt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260906-ready-to-talk-german-far-right-celebrates-victory</link><description>
"Everything is possible" was the campaign slogan of the Alternative for Germany (AfD) in Saxony-Anhalt, where the far-right party has won a landslide election victory, although they appear short of a majority in the state parliament. Ulrich Siegmund, who is in pole position to become the state leader, knows he has history in his grasp. We get reaction from CSU MP Tobias Winkler.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9f9acea0-aa18-11f1-8daf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Ulrich-Siegmund.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9f9acea0-aa18-11f1-8daf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Ulrich-Siegmund.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bdc4c90-aa11-11f1-bf15-fd184c2e2b2f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 17:32:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany’s far-right AfD wins big in key state election but falls short of majority</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest</link><description>
Germany’s far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party headed towards a landslide victory in state ​elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in its bid to form the country's first far-right state government since World War II. However, final results showed AfD falling three seats short of an absolute majority, with 39 lawmakers in an 83-member parliament.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/727d2c16-aa12-11f1-ac8b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249584038776-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/727d2c16-aa12-11f1-ac8b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249584038776-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f25a936a-aa0d-11f1-81e7-1dee8a48d84d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 16:15:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/727d2c16-aa12-11f1-ac8b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249584038776-1.jpg">© Michael Kappeler, DPA via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: Nepal rescue operations, World Nomad Games and Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
From the desperate search for workers trapped in the hydropower tunnels buried by the catastrophic flooding in Nepal to crowds of women mourning the victims of a US bombardment of a wedding in southern Iran, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dea2950c-a9bd-11f1-b557-b7773d79cef0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 14:21:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg">© Athit Perawongmetha, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'A bad sign': US envoys head to Kyiv after three-hour talks with Putin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/a-bad-sign-us-envoys-head-to-kyiv-after-three-hour-talks-with-putin</link><description>
As US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner head to Kyiv following what the White House described as "substantive" talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin, FRANCE 24 correspondent Gulliver Cragg talks about what he describes as a climate of scepticism in Ukraine that these latest negotiations could bring a long-awaited breakthrough.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51c556be-a9b9-11f1-a995-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-070111-070526-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51c556be-a9b9-11f1-a995-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-070111-070526-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">565fcc18-a9b9-11f1-907c-275248e6db97</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 06:18:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany's far-right AfD eyes historic state victory in Saxony-Anhalt election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-eyes-historic-state-victory-in-saxony-anhalt-election</link><description>
Germany's anti-immigrant Alternative for Germany party is aiming to become the first far-right party to take power at a state level since World War II as voters in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt head to the polls Sunday. However, a failure to secure an absolute majority may see the politically isolated party struggle to form a government. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4191ae4-a9b2-11f1-9431-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-05T175805Z-834783995-RC25DNA1ZV3U-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-AFD-RALLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4191ae4-a9b2-11f1-9431-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-05T175805Z-834783995-RC25DNA1ZV3U-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-AFD-RALLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">533da8b8-a9b2-11f1-af2b-b91a3278f929</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 05:52:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4191ae4-a9b2-11f1-9431-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-05T175805Z-834783995-RC25DNA1ZV3U-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-AFD-RALLY.jpg">© Fabrizio Bensch, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>After meeting with US envoys in Kyiv, Zelensky says war likely to ‘continue in winter’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-live-trump-s-envoys-head-to-ukraine-after-substantive-talks-with-putin</link><description>
Although Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky described talks with US special envoy Steve Witkoff and Donald Trump’s son-in-law Jared Kushner as “substantial”, he warned that the war with Russia was likely to continue this winter. The US envoys arrived in Kyiv for their first official visit on Sunday, a day after meeting Russia’s President Vladimir Putin in Moscow. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
